{"case_id":"C055","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"change_types":["new entry points or features","attack-surface expansion"],"affected_functions":["plist_from_json","plist_to_json","plist_from_memory"],"reason":"The commit adds a new JSON parser and serializer, but the existing fuzzers invoke only plist_from_bin and plist_from_xml. Consequently, arbitrary JSON input does not reach the new plist_from_json/jsmn parsing path, and the build wiring creates no JSON fuzz target. Although plist_from_memory now dispatches inputs beginning with '[' or '{' to JSON, neither existing harness calls plist_from_memory.","evidence":["include/plist/plist.h adds the public APIs plist_from_json and plist_to_json.","src/jplist.c introduces the JSON parsing implementation, including jsmn_parse, parse_object, parse_array, parse_string, and parse_primitive.","plist_from_memory gains a JSON branch for inputs whose first byte is '[' or '{'.","bplist_fuzzer.cc directly calls plist_from_bin, while xplist_fuzzer.cc directly calls plist_from_xml.","The OSS-Fuzz build loop includes only bplist_fuzzer and xplist_fuzzer."],"recommended_action":"Add and build a JSON fuzz target that passes arbitrary byte buffers and lengths directly to plist_from_json and frees any returned plist. Consider exercising plist_to_json, including both prettify values, on successfully parsed trees; add an appropriate JSON seed corpus and dictionary if available."}
